{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-09-30T23:29:18.917Z","data":{"text":"Done. All four task files (three source/test files in scope plus the new module) are implemented, and both the task verify and the proposal verify pass.\n\nSummary of work:\n\n- **`src/cli/plan-steer.ts`** (new): `readSteeringPlan(projectRoot, config, name)` locates a change with `findChange`, derives its state from the change's own tree, and returns the located change, id, and `## Steering` section. Returns `null` for no match or a checkout change without `steering`; throws the cli-foundation refusal for an approved worktree/stacked change with none. The section uses `deriveSteering` order, `describeTrigger`, `steeringMarkerPath`, and `parseFrontmatter` bodies.\n- **`src/cli/plan.ts`**: calls `readSteeringPlan` before `findSpecFolder`, appends the section to the built prompt, writes it as the handoff `plan-prompt.md`, and passes the change's tree root to `spawnInteractive` and `readPlanningUsage`. Stays at 230 lines.\n- **`src/cli/lint.ts`**: explicit ids now resolve through `findChange` first with a `findSpecFolder` fallback; linting still uses `cwd` as project root and one `cwd` import graph.\n- **`tests/steering-plan.test.ts`** (new): covers the three planning scenarios plus \"Lint a change in its worktree\" against a temp git repo with a change approved into a worktree.\n\nVerification:\n- `node --import tsx --test tests/steering-plan.test.ts` → 4 pass\n- `pnpm verify` → exit 0\n\nResult written to `openspec/changes/128-steering-triggers/.run/results/3.md`.\n\nTouched: src/cli/plan.ts, src/cli/plan-steer.ts, src/cli/lint.ts, tests/steering-plan.test.ts"}}
